 ("h2", "5. Underemployment and Unemployment"),
 ("p", "Take Laxmi, a farmer with two hectares of unirrigated land growing jowar and arhar. All five family members work in the plot throughout the year because they have nowhere else to go. Everyone is working, yet each works less than their potential: this is **underemployment** (disguised unemployment), hidden unlike open unemployment, where a person without a job is clearly visible. If two members work elsewhere, production on the farm will not suffer and family income rises. Underemployment can also be seen in cities among casual workers (painters, plumbers, repair persons) who do not find work daily and among those on streets pushing carts."),
